  "notes": "Primary and JSS make up the nine years of Universal Basic Education. A 2025 proposal for twelve uninterrupted years of basic education, without the JSS/SSS split, had not been put in place: the curricula NERDC released in September 2025 still start at Primary 1, Primary 4, JSS 1 and SS 1. The Basic 7–9 names for JSS are common but not in the cited pages. Early childhood care and development education (ECCDE) is for children of 3 to 5 and is not compulsory; schools name its years Nursery 1, Nursery 2 and Kindergarten (also Nursery 3 or KG), the last being the one pre-primary year."
